{"content":[{"c":["PALTI"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of the 12 spies Moses sent to explore the land of Canaan before the Israelite conquest. Palti represented Benjamin’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Num.13.9","r":"Num.13.9","rawR":"Num.13.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.13.9","value":"Num.13.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 13:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Laish’s son, to whom King Saul gave Michal, his daughter and David’s wife, after the break between Saul and David (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.25.44","r":"1Sam.25.44","rawR":"1Sam.25.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.25.44","value":"1Sam.25.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 25:44"},"). Michal was recovered from him and returned to David (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.3.15","r":"2Sam.3.15","rawR":"2Sam.3.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.3.15","value":"2Sam.3.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 3:15"},"); in that reference he is called Paltiel."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Palti","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 13:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.13.9","rawQueryValue":"Num.13.9","sourceRefExact":"Num.13.9"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 25:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.25.44","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.25.44","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.25.44"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 3:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.3.15","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.3.15","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.3.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e181752dcc1512985981ea62c7b8a1311322418930382a7c077c94a3783601c0","sourceItemName":"Palti","sourceItemOrder":20,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Palti","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Palti","title":"Palti","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}